    "narrative": "Today\u2019s Austin Waves lineup is anchored by **Kyle Tucker**, whose 85.90 efficiency score makes him our clear-cut priority start against Feltner. While **Kyle Tucker** is batting seventh, the combination of a favorable 5.05 xERA matchup and a massive park boost more than compensates for the order penalty. Similarly, **Luis Robert Jr.** (77.40) and **Andy Pages** (74.43) represent our most potent outfield upside, both benefiting from high-tier SP skill matchups against Ray and Feltner, respectively. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** also projects as an elite secondary option at 73.66; his 14% dynamic platoon boost against Baz suggests he is primed to capitalize on a favorable pitching delivery that enhances his run-production potential.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved our bench, where **Miguel Vargas** was the odd man out with a score of 54.27. While **Miguel Vargas** offers an excellent xwOBA of 0.383 and some sneaky stolen base utility against Gausman, his path to productivity is obstructed by the high-floor performance of **Sam Antonacci** and **Gunnar Henderson**. The optimizer prioritized the latter duo due to superior park factors and the current wind conditions favoring **Sam Antonacci**. While **Nasim Nunez** (59.42) remains a marginal start, his inclusion is strictly driven by our need to chase stolen bases, as his ability to exploit Quantrill's slow delivery outweighs the positional scarcity issues we are currently navigating. \n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the 37% rain risk for the games featuring **Andy Pages** and **Kyle Tucker**; any delay or cancellation could significantly kneecap our daily output. Conversely, while **Liam Hicks** (46.44) and **Jackson Merrill** (55.17) are hovering near the bottom of our efficiency thresholds, they remain locked in to ensure we maintain our plate appearance consistency. We continue to monitor the progress of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson** on the IL, as their return remains critical to stabilizing the middle of our order and pushing us back toward the top of the league standings.",
